# `issue-27282-move-match-input-into-guard` WAS NEVER A DEFECT. Its port had deleted
# the closure AND the `&mut bool` scrutinee and matched a struct by value; with the
# upstream construct restored logosc refuses with "cannot move 'b' while it is
# borrowed". It is now a fail fixture under tests/imported/fail/nll/. Two controls
# separate the mechanism: a guard that moves nothing compiles, and the same guard
# without the closure gives the identical sentence — the refusal is the scrutinee
# loan, not the closure.
