#       PARAMETER whose TYPE IS A REFERENCE. Separating pair, differing only in the
#       parameter's type: `fn f(b: &i64) { g(&mut b); }` ADMITS, `fn f(b: i64) { g(&mut b); }`
#       is REFUSED "cannot borrow 'b' as mutable: not declared as mut". A non-mut LOCAL
#       of type `&mut i64` is also refused, and ASSIGNMENT to a non-mut `&mut` parameter
