#              u64 = &y;` inside `call1<'a>` ADMITS; only `return z;` refuses, and by a
#              SYNTACTIC dangling-local rule. A let annotation naming a free region is
#              not a constraint on its initializer.
#   lifereg.C  SPLITS INTO TWO, each with its own pair:
#     NEW-CAPFRAME (regions-nested-fns-2) a closure returning a borrow of its OWN local
#              is REFUSED (`cannot return reference to local variable 'w'`); the same
#              closure returning a borrow of the ENCLOSING fn's local is ADMITTED. The
