# ⚠ THE ROOTS WERE RE-CHECKED AGAINST THE RESTORED CONSTRUCTS AND ALL THREE
# HANDED-DOWN GROUPINGS SPLIT. `bck.C`/`nllmoves.C` ("the closure boundary
# deposits nothing") is FOUR mechanisms, each with its own one-variable pair:
#   NEW-CAPLOAN  a loan CROSSING the boundary deposits nothing. `id(&g)` REFUSED
#                vs `(|| &g)()` ADMITTED; and `c.push(&mut y)` twice REFUSED vs
#                the same two loans minted by captures ADMITTED.
#   NEW-CAPMOVE  a `move` capture's move-ness comes from the USE FORM inside the
#                body, not the keyword. On ONE program: `move || { *v }` ADMITS,
#                `move || { eat(v) }` REFUSED "cannot move 'v' while it is borrowed".
#   NEW-CESC     an escaping closure's region is constrained ONLY by a `dyn`
#                coercion. Boxed REFUSED vs a plain generic `keep<F>(f:F)->F`
#                ADMITTED. This is also why the two bucket-1 rows refuse.
#   NEW-CMUT     ⛔ CLOSED 2026-09-12b, its ONE row. It was never a closure-
