#                already fired at a generic `F: Fn` bound. What was missing is
#                the ARRIVAL — a `-> impl Trait` RETURN bound was adopted
#                unchecked at sema_decl.cpp, and the return-position branch of
#                `resolve_type` never read the bound's args at all. Both ends
#                repaired; the declared bound is now checked against the hidden
#                type by the same reader a type-param bound uses.
# ⚠ A closure body is NOT opaque: a loan minted and used inside one is tracked
#   ("cannot assign to 'g' because it is borrowed"). bck.C as written was wrong
#   about the mechanism, not only about the grouping.
