# The 2026-09-07 merge rests on TWO pairs, one per block letter, and a pair
# speaks for the row it was written from. "A temporary has no owner to key a loan
# on" is a SYMPTOM the two populations share, and a shared symptom is not a
# shared defect (2026-08-27: 10 rows grouped by one instrument reading, the fix
# closed 1). Whoever prices this block prices it as 3 + 4, or measures the merge
# with a pair per row.
# ── 2026-09-08 — SIX ROWS RETURN FROM `bc_admits_blocked.ledger`, THE WHOLE ────
#    `BUCKET-3 DIVERGENCE-DROP` GROUP, BECAUSE THE OWNER RETIRED THE CLAUSE
#
# The owner decided on 2026-09-08 that Logos's drop semantics are Rust-canonical:
# `Drop::drop` takes `&mut self`, and moving a sub-value out of a value that
# implements `Drop` is E0509 and REFUSED. The spec clause that blessed these six,
# `intrinsic.drop.skip-moved-out-paths`, is rewritten the same day and now covers
# only NON-`Drop` owners (Rust's own drop-flag behaviour, not a divergence); the
# refusal is the new clause `intrinsic.drop.move-out-of-drop-type-refused`.
#
# ALL SIX MOVE BECAUSE OF THE CLAUSE — derived from the blocked file by direct
# listing, and no row of the six had a second reason to be filed there. THREE of
# them carry an ADDITIONAL blocker that the clause's retirement does NOT remove,
# and each says so on its own row: `--r13`/`--t13` move a field whose type A16
# structural auto-Copy makes `Copy`, so no move is seen at all (zero fires under
# the E0509 door, reason UNCHANGED since 2026-08-28), and `move-error-with-note--b`
# uses the `match` struct-pattern door.
#
# 91 -> 97. THE ACTIONABLE LEDGER GROWING HERE IS THE CORRECT RESULT: these are
# real defects again, and a ledger that hid them would be lying about the language.
borrowck-move-out-of-tuple-struct-with-dtor--r13 bck.NEW-A16 tests/imported/admit/borrowck/borrowck-move-out-of-tuple-struct-with-dtor--r13  # 2026-09-08 RETURNED from bc_admits_blocked (was BUCKET-3 DIVERGENCE-DROP). ⚠ SECOND BLOCKER, unchanged from the 2026-08-28 record and re-verified 2026-09-08: the moved field has type `struct Inner { a: i64 }`, which DIVERGENCES A16 structural auto-Copy makes `Copy`, so the checker sees NO MOVE at all (zero E0509 fires). Retiring the drop clause does not reach it; A16 does. Its own body also exits 1 with DROPS=0 (`impl Drop for S` never runs) — that soundness_queue row (letstruct_destructure_skips_user_drop) was CLOSED 2026-09-08 and its program is now tests/logos/fail/letstruct_destructure_drop_owner_e0509.logos; the DROPS=0 residual here is A16's, not that row's
