# ── 2026-09-08 — FOUR OF THE SIX CLOSED THE SAME DAY THEY RETURNED ──────────
# The E0509 landing refuses all four, at three separate doors (dotted path,
# field-init from a base, FRU) plus the `match` struct-pattern door, and each is
# now a FAIL fixture under tests/imported/fail/borrowck/ with its sentence pinned
# in full. 97 -> 93. The two `--r13`/`--t13` rows stay, with root `bck.NEW-A16`
# and the number that condemns them: ZERO fires, because their moved field is
# `struct Inner { a: i64 }` and structural auto-Copy calls it Copy, so the
# checker sees no move at all. A16 is what must move, not the E0509 rule.
# ── 2026-09-08, AN UNPREDICTED CLOSING, REPORTED AS ONE ─────────────────────
# `issue-52059-report-when-borrow-and-drop-conflict` is REFUSED by the E0509
# landing and is now a fail fixture under tests/imported/fail/nll/. It was NOT in
# that landing's prediction file. Its construct is
# `fn finish_1(s: S) -> &mut i64 { return s.url; }`, which rustc also refuses as
# E0509 before E0713 applies — so the refusal is correct and the port is illegal.
# ⚠ ITS ROOT IS NOT CLOSED. The row was nllmoves.E, an E0713 hole: a `&mut`
# handed out PAST a destructor that then writes through it. That hole is now
# UNREACHABLE THROUGH THIS PROGRAM and needs a carrier that does not move a field
# out of a Drop value — unrowed_backlog entry
# `e0713_mutref_past_destructor_needs_a_new_carrier`. 93 -> 92.
# ── 2026-09-11 — 90 -> 87. `lifereg.NEW-E0207` CLOSES WHOLE, AND THE CLASS WAS ──
#    ENUMERATED BY A COMPILER CENSUS RATHER THAN BY A GREP
#
# THE ARM. One predicate in `lower_impl_block` (src/compiler/sema_decl.cpp): an
# impl LIFETIME binder that one of the impl's own ASSOCIATED-TYPE definitions
# names, and that is mentioned nowhere in the impl HEADER, is E0207-unconstrained.
# "Mentioned in the header" is ONE recursive walk over the impl node with the
# binder list and the body excluded — so `&'a mut S`, `W<'a>` and `Tr2<W<'a>>`
# all constrain, and the trait-argument lifetime that sema_decl's resolve loop
# discards by design ("Logos doesn't track regions structurally for trait
# dispatch") is carried by construction rather than by a second special case.
#
# THE CLASS, BY THE PROPERTY, WITH THE NUMBER. A census counter at the site,
# over 9839 `.logos` files (tests + stdlib + examples) and 6,341,664 impl-lowering
# arrivals: SEVEN unconstrained binders named by an associated type, FOURTEEN
# unconstrained binders NOT named by one — Rust permits those and so does the arm
# — and ZERO unconstrained TYPE parameters. The type half of E0207 is therefore
# DECLINED on a measured population of 0 and not on a reading: it closes no row
# here and no soundness_queue row, and its only instance is a hand program.
#
# WHAT THE HEADER WALK IS NOT. `WHERE` counts as CONSTRAINING. Rust's rule is
# narrower — an outlives predicate does not constrain, only a projection
# predicate does — and with no rustc on this box the two cannot be told apart
# here. The conservative direction is ADMIT, so this is a named under-refusal,
# not a divergence claim, and a `where`-only E0207 stays open.
#
# ⚠ THE BLAME HEADER WAS THE BLOCKER, AND IT IS FIXED AT THIS SITE ONLY.
# `lower_impl_block` sets neither `ctx_` nor `node_line_`, so its diagnostics
# inherit whatever the last function lowered left behind — the pricing round's
# arm printed at line 557 of a 40-line file and blamed a stdlib function. The
# landing sets both around the refusal. The GENERAL defect is unchanged and is
# the standing soundness_queue row `e0184_blame_header_names_unrelated_impl`.
# TOTAL 81


